the comments.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.890
Just to get the party started here are my
TOP 10 Sherlock Moments So Far:

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.360
Number 10 - Jim From IT during the great game

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.940
I was totally fooled the first time I met
Jim from IT, the scene takes a whole different

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.950
context once you find out Jim is really James.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.880
It’s a perfect blend of the unintentional
humor of Sherlock breaking down a person’s

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.329
attributes, Moriarty baiting him with a false
identity and onlookers like Molly and Watson

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:07.570
completely embarrassed by the whole experience.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.640
It’s awkward Sherlock comedy at it’s best.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.780
9 The Mind Palace from the Hound of Baskerville.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.720
I love how Watson is always making fun of
Sherlock for not knowing loose facts about

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.950
mundane things.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.640
The Mind Palace is his answer to all that.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.700
If you’re not familiar with memory enhancement,
it’s a real thing.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.869
They’re called mnemonic devices and they
give people ways to store large amounts of

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:30.409
information in their brains.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:33.440
The other side of that is recall devices and
memory triggers.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.360
Storing memories using mnemonic devices is
one thing, but using a word or a smell or

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.150
a phrase to recall a memory is the key to
finding things inside the mind palace.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:42.780
When you see the graphics pop up around Sherlock’s
head, what you’re seeing are his recall

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.680
devices that help him find the information
he’s looking for inside his head.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.960
8 Whipping the corpse during a study in pink.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.400
This was our first introduction to Benedict
Cumberbatch’s sherlock.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.790
It totally explained the character in a few
strokes of the riding crop.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:59.560
Unlike Robert Downey Jr’s vagabond savant
approach to the character, Cumberbatch’s

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:05.159
Sherlock is hyper focused, intense and deceptively
asexual.

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:08.780
If you ever wanted to explain sherlock to
someone who had never seen it before.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.289
Just show them this scene.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:13.170
7 The very bloody mess during Hound of Baskerville.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:17.280
The episode itself wasn’t my favorite, but
the reason I loved this moment so much was

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.150
that it gave you a real sense that some of
their most epic cases were happening in between

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.270
episodes.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:28.489
All it takes is one look at sherlock covered
in blood and a few cursory words about having

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:32.770
to ride the tube and your mind explodes into
this pocket universe where we actually get

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.490
to see the case he just worked.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.341
I like to think of it as the greater tales
of Sherlock as told by watson via his blog.

00:02:38.341 --> 00:02:39.341
If you’re not familiar with the Conan Doyle
Sherlock stories, most of them are told in

00:02:39.341 --> 00:02:40.341
first person by Watson as if being told after
they had all happened.

00:02:40.341 --> 00:02:41.341
So Watson’s blog is the current version
of the character slowly writing the conan

00:02:41.341 --> 00:02:42.341
doyle book The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes.

00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:43.470
For anyone that’s curious, that bloody spear
is a reference to the conan doyle story The

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.880
Adventures of Black Peter.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.180
6 Sherlock’s Standoff With Moriarty in The
Great Game.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.879
I loved the way this episode ended and the
ambiguity of Sherlock’s intentions.

00:02:51.879 --> 00:02:57.220
It’s always a game of chess with those two,
but would he have shot the explosives if Moriarty

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.599
had called his bluff?

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:03.100
After seeing how fast Sherlock’s mind works
in Scandal in Belgravia I definitely think

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.860
he had formulated a plan of how to survive
the explosion had he pulled the trigger.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:14.170
That idea, planning for catastrophic events,
is crucial to how he survived the fall in

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.170
reichenbach fall.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.569
5 Irene Adler’s Battle Suit in Scandal in
Belgravia.

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:22.260
It’s not so much the suit that was memorable,
it was Irene watching sherlock try to break

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.430
her down, while she was breaking him down.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:29.530
The universe tells us that these two people
need to be together, but because of who they

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:36.550
are it ultimately ends in tragedy, even though
I felt the ending of the episode was optimistic.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:41.330
Or at least left room for her return.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:45.720
Amanda Abbington as Mary Morstan during season
3 is going to have a hard time matching Laura

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.190
Pulver’s Irene in season 2.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.239
4 Buckingham Palace and pants during A Scandal
In Belgravia.

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:54.629
So many moments from this episode, but the
bedsheet and the banter with Mycroft was so

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:55.810
much fun.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:00.209
Just like the explosives in great game and
the roof jump in reichenbach fall, I definitely

00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:02.690
think he would have just keep walking.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:04.650
And casually strolled out of buckingham palace
naked.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:09.129
Let me know below in the comments how far
you think sherlock would have walked outside

00:04:09.129 --> 00:04:12.099
naked before the queens guard tackled him.

00:04:12.099 --> 00:04:15.280
3 Moriarty steals the Crown Jewels in Reichenbach
fall.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:22.060
You don’t get to see a lot of Moriarty’s
process, but I loved the way he was so casual

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.650
about the whole thing.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.270
Once you learn why he did it that part becomes
less of a mystery, but no one on this show

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.680
has more fun than Moriarty.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.599
Sherlock and Watson have fun and Sherlock
definitely feels this intense satisfaction

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:39.099
when he solves puzzles, but I don’t think
he experiences pure joy in the way Moriarty

00:04:39.099 --> 00:04:43.030
does when he’s misbehaving.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:47.479
That would make a great spinoff show, Boys
Misbehaving starring Andrew Scott.

00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:49.879
2 The Rooftop Fall in Reichenbach Fall.

00:04:49.879 --> 00:04:52.139
You really do feel like it’s the end.

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:57.139
But the experience of the explosives in scandal
and the bedsheet and all of sherlock’s other

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:01.259
gambits kind of make you feel like he’s
going to get up and dust himself off.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:04.070
So when I saw him lying there on the pavement
my heart kind of leapt out of my throat.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.159
The whole episode had this air of finality
to it, mostly because of the watson scene

00:05:06.159 --> 00:05:08.550
at the beginning, but also because when they
filmed it the series hadn’t been renewed

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.999
for a third yet.

00:05:09.999 --> 00:05:14.379
So you didn’t know what was going to happen.

00:05:14.379 --> 00:05:16.889
I’ll actually be doing a separate video
breaking down how I think he survived the

00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:17.889
fall.

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:21.419
and my number one moment The Reveal at Sherlock’s
Grave in Reichenbach fall.

00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:26.159
You had just gone through this intense experience,
so when the camera pans away to a very much

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:29.550
alive sherlock it was this giant WTF moment.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.490
Remember, the series hadn’t been renewed
yet, so people had no idea if the fall would

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:34.490
ever be explained.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.020
Just FYI though, that will not be the case
this season.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:41.529
I mean, I totally expect it to end on a huge
cliffhanger, but both benedict cumberbatch

00:05:41.529 --> 00:05:44.589
and martin freeman are under contract for
a fourth series.

00:05:44.589 --> 00:05:48.130
But no filming date has been announced, so
hopefully we won’t have to wait two more

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.289
years like last time.

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:55.720
Like I said, I’ll be doing a breakdown of
how I think he survived the fall tomorrow.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.360
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

